{"schema_version":"1.0.0","metadata":{"trial_id":"202610081400-old-west-saloon-effort-high","prompting_method_id":"concept-build-free.v0","model_id":"claude-sonnet-5-5","seed":11,"server_state_id":"concept-free.v1"},"style":{"name":"Old West frontier saloon","rationale":"Second pass fixes the flat, boxy first build. Depth: dark-timber piers stand proud of the wall, the two wide centre bays are recessed, windows are set back with open shutters, and the cornice and eaves overhang. The front is framed by a continuous beam band at y=4, 5, 9 and 13, so the pale polished_andesite panels read as infill between dark timber. The roofline is resolved by a tall false front with a birch signboard, wall signs and a cornice, plus stepped side returns and a spruce shed roof with stair eaves that hides behind it. The ground floor is an open boardwalk with a hitching rail, hay, a water cauldron and barrels, and batwing doors recessed into the centre bay. The balcony wraps the front and both ends with a fence rail, a door and a red banner, and lanterns mark the entrance. Both long sides get recessed windows and corner posts, and the back is plain with one door and four windows. The palette hierarchy is kept: andesite dominant, dark oak timber supporting, spruce for floors, and lantern, birch and red as the only accents."},"palette":{"manifest":["minecraft:polished_andesite","minecraft:dark_oak_planks","minecraft:stripped_dark_oak_log","minecraft:dark_oak_fence","minecraft:spruce_planks","minecraft:spruce_slab","minecraft:spruce_stairs","minecraft:dark_oak_slab","minecraft:glass_pane","minecraft:birch_planks","minecraft:oak_wall_sign","minecraft:lantern","minecraft:red_wall_banner","minecraft:dark_oak_door","minecraft:spruce_trapdoor","minecraft:dark_oak_trapdoor","minecraft:hay_bale","minecraft:water_cauldron","minecraft:barrel"]},"placements":[{"op":"fill","from":[0,0,0],"to":[13,0,15],"block":"minecraft:spruce_planks"},{"op":"fill","from":[-1,0,-3],"to":[14,0,-1],"block":"minecraft